/*!
\page page_strpsromanpot StRpsRomanPot

\brief A single Roman Pot detector station housing four silicon planes and two PMT timing detectors.

\section rpsromanpot_overview Overview

StRpsRomanPot is a station-level container for the **Roman Pot System (RPS)**.
Each of the eight stations (indexed 0–7) holds four silicon strip detector planes and
two scintillator/PMT timing detectors.  The class stores the PMT ADC/TAC values and
a status flag for the whole station.

**Detector**: Roman Pot System (RPS / pp2pp)  
**Stage**: Station-level container

\section rpsromanpot_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StRpsRomanPot
\endcode

\code
StRpsCollection → StRpsRomanPot[0..7] → StRpsPlane[0..3] → StRpsCluster
\endcode

\section rpsromanpot_members Data Members

| Type | Member | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| \c StRpsPlane[4] | \c mPlanes | Array of four silicon strip detector planes |
| \c UChar_t | \c mRomanPotId | Roman Pot index (0–7) |
| \c UChar_t | \c mStatus | Station status flag (0 = good) |
| \c UInt_t[2] | \c mAdc | ADC values from the two PMT scintillator timing detectors |
| \c UInt_t[2] | \c mTac | TAC values from the two PMT scintillator timing detectors |

\section rpsromanpot_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c romanPotId() | Roman Pot index (0–7) |
| \c numberOfPlanes() | Always 4 |
| \c numberOfPlanesWithClusters() | Planes with at least one cluster |
| \c adc(i) | ADC of PMT i (0 or 1) |
| \c tac(i) | TAC of PMT i (0 or 1) |
| \c status() | Station status flag |
| \c plane(i) | Pointer to plane i (0–3) |

\section rpsromanpot_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StRpsRomanPot* rp = rpsColl->romanPot(irp);
if (rp->status() != 0) continue;
unsigned int nActive = rp->numberOfPlanesWithClusters();
unsigned int tac0 = rp->tac(0); // PMT 0 timing
for (unsigned int ip = 0; ip < rp->numberOfPlanes(); ++ip) {
    const StRpsPlane* plane = rp->plane(ip);
    // ... process clusters
}
\endcode

\see StRpsPlane, StRpsCluster, StRpsCollection
*/
